    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "Parts a to c are direct cosine-rule angle calculations with the same two sides and a changing third side. The cosine values are positive, zero and negative, which scaffolds a pattern. Part d is the hardest demand. Without finding any angle, the student must carry the pattern over to a new triangle, identify 12 as the longest side, compare 7²+9² with 12², and interpret the negative sign of the cosine numerator as obtuse. This is a mild generalisation with some signposting, so it sits above routine linked cosine-rule procedures but well below non-trivial reframing.",
